>>> read ok {"path":"package.json"}
{
  "name": "dashboard",
  "scripts": {
    "build": "npm run build:types && npm run build:app",
    "build:types": "tsc -p tsconfig.json",
    "build:app": "vite build"
  }
}
>>> read ok {"path":"tsconfig.json"}
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "incremental": false,
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true
  },
  "include": ["src", "scripts", "node_modules/@internal/**/*"]
}
>>> final
Two things make the build slow. First, `build:types` runs `tsc` over `node_modules/@internal/**/*` because that folder is in `include`, so every internal package is type-checked on every build. Second, `incremental` is `false`, so nothing is reused between runs. Dropping the `node_modules` entry from `include` and turning on `incremental` should cut most of the type-check time; `vite build` itself is not the bottleneck here.
